    "q-350412": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350412",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices above, write the following expression as a Hadamard product. Here $(\\,\\cdot \\,)$ denotes matrix multiplication.\n\n| $(AB)\\cdot (By)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $⊙$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-6$ |  |  | $4$ |  |  |  |  |",
      "worked_solution": "The Hadamard product of two compatible vectors $u$ and $v$ can be expressed as the matrix product\n\n$$\nv⊙u=\\text{diag}(v)u.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nBy=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(AB)\\cdot (By) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\text{diag}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}])[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]⊙[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
