    "q-350493": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350493",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nA⊙B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,A⊙C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nfind $A⊙(B+C).$",
      "worked_solution": "For compatible matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ and scalar $\\alpha ,$ the Hadamard product has the following properties:\n\n- Commutativity:\n\n$$\nA⊙B=B⊙A\n$$\n\n- Associativity:\n\n$$\n(A⊙B)⊙C=A⊙(B⊙C)\n$$\n\n- Distributivity over Addition:\n\n$$\nA⊙(B+C)=A⊙B+A⊙C\n$$\n\n- Scalar Distributivity:\n\n$$\n\\alpha (A⊙B)=(\\alpha A)⊙B=A⊙(\\alpha B)\n$$\n\nIn this case, by the distributivity over the addition of the Hadamard product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A⊙(B+C) & =A⊙B+A⊙C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+5 & 4+(-3) \\\\ 3+2 & -2+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
