    "q-350504": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350504",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nA⊙B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,A⊙C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nfind $A⊙(B+C)+A⊙(B⊙C).$",
      "worked_solution": "For compatible matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ and scalar $\\alpha ,$ the Hadamard product has the following properties:\n\n- Commutativity:\n\n$$\nA⊙B=B⊙A\n$$\n\n- Associativity:\n\n$$\n(A⊙B)⊙C=A⊙(B⊙C)\n$$\n\n- Distributivity over Addition:\n\n$$\nA⊙(B+C)=A⊙B+A⊙C\n$$\n\n- Scalar Distributivity:\n\n$$\n\\alpha (A⊙B)=(\\alpha A)⊙B=A⊙(\\alpha B)\n$$\n\nIn this case, by the associativity and distributivity over addition of the Hadamard product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A⊙(B+C)+A⊙(B⊙C) & =A⊙B+A⊙C+(A⊙B)⊙C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]⊙[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+4 & 2+6 \\\\ 1+6 & 3+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-350504-a",
